\title{Warning}
\taxon{Remark}
\date{2022-10-01}
\author{JB00}
\import{macros}

\p{We used the complex structure to make sure that there is an eval (which is a priori complex valued). In general, a real valued orthogonal matrix (#{AA^T = \mathrm{Id}}) \em{cannot} be diagonalised over #{\mathbb{R}}. E.g. the rotation map in #{\mathbb{R}^2},}

##{A = \begin{pmatrix} \cos\alpha & -\sin\alpha \\ \sin\alpha & \cos\alpha \end{pmatrix}, \qquad \chi_A(\lambda) = \begin{vmatrix} \cos\alpha - \lambda & -\sin\alpha \\ \sin\alpha & \cos\alpha - \lambda \end{vmatrix} = (\cos\alpha - \lambda)^2 + \sin^2\alpha,}

\p{so #{\lambda = e^{\pm i\alpha} \notin \mathbb{R}} generically.}
